# What `docker build` must NOT carry.
#
# `deploy.yml` builds with `context: .`, so without this file the daemon hashes
# the entire working tree. On a developer's machine that is 37 GB — 34 GB of it
# `apps/desktop/src-tauri/target`, 2.6 GB of iOS build output — none of which
# the backend image has any use for. CI's checkout is clean, so this was
# invisible there and painful everywhere else.
#
# It also means a `.env` kept beside the code can never enter a build context,
# and therefore never enter the GitHub Actions layer cache. The published image
# is already clean — inspected 2026-08-23, only PATH, NODE_VERSION,
# YARN_VERSION, NODE_ENV and GIT_SHA, no key material — and this keeps it that
# way by construction rather than by luck.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluding `apps/desktop`, `apps/mobile` or `apps/admin`
# wholesale: the Dockerfile COPYs each of their `package.json` files, because
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` against a workspace lockfile needs every
# workspace's manifest to resolve. Only their heavy subdirectories go.

# Dependency trees and build output. `apps/backend` is COPY'd wholesale and
# rebuilt inside the image, so anything here is overwritten at best, stale at
# worst — and is a different platform's binaries at least some of the time.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo

# `*.tsbuildinfo` is not housekeeping — it is the reason this file had to exist
# before anyone noticed it was missing. `tsc -p tsconfig.json` is incremental:
# with the host's `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` in the context it decides the project
# is already built and emits nothing, and the build only survived because the
# host's `dist/` came along too. So a local `docker build` was shipping the
# developer's compiled output rather than compiling. CI never saw it — a fresh
# checkout has neither file. Excluding `dist` without this turns that silent
# substitution into a loud `TS7016: Could not find a declaration file`.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The two directories that account for ~36 of the 37 GB.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/vendor

.git
coverage
*.log

# Secrets and local state, belt and braces. None of these are tracked, which is
# exactly why a build context is where they would otherwise turn up.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.keystore
